      "writtenOn": "2022-08-19T21:32:03Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I see where you\u0027re going here, but honestly, I find this harder to read. Because the struct is just a bunch of ints, the only way I have to parse the values is to constantly refer back to the definition as I read each instance. Adding newlines makes the instances take up more vertical space, so now I have to scroll up and down while I read.\n\nI\u0027d prefer it if the struct members were initialized using `.member \u003d val` syntax, so I wouldn\u0027t have to refer to the definition to parse the instances. (I think this is what you suggested.) If you do that, I don\u0027t think it will make a huge difference whether each member goes on its own line, and I\u0027d probably be satisfied with whatever `clang-format` came up with.\n\nIt would also be nice if the members that should only be 0 or 1 were `bool`s.",
      "parentUuid": "d7585108_f633f70d",
      "revId": "de8418df73cb3f27fc7f62034483f46a17508e38",
